connected to it, 2 ST32550W (2Go) and 1 ST34371W (4Go) (Seagate).

My problem is that the hard drives aren't seen by the Alpha.

My plan was to modify the SCSI chain to re-order the disks (4Go at id 0, 
the 2 Go at 1 and 2, the cdrom at 3), and before i began the 2 ST32550 
disks were recognized by the system (as scsi id 1 and 2). Now, no one of 
the 3 disks are recognized, only the CDROM, even when i plug only one 
disk on the computer.

When i type 'show dev' on the SRM console prompt there is only 
dka400.4.0.9.0, the CDROM, and pka0.7.9.0 the QLogic ISP1020 controller 
(there is also dva0 and ewa0 but this isn't of interest here), but not 
the disks connected to the system.

When i type "show config" on the SRM console prompt i don't see the disks.

The only spot where i can see the disks is in the boot configuration of 
the ARC console, but their names are constituted of strange characters, 
not the model and name of the drives, as it does for the CDROM (an HP 
C4325).

I have checked the disks on one of my others i386 boxes and they are 
properly recognized: i can do a fdisk on them, they appear as 
/dev/sda... but the partition table cannot be read by my PC (i suppose 
that this is normal ?).

I have double checked my SCSI chain, but even when there is only one 
SCSI disk connected (no other hard disks or CDROM connected) i don't see 
the disk.

I have tried to use "isp_edit -sd" to reinitialize the nvram of the 
controller (if i have correctly understand) but with no visible effects.

Also i have searched without success the "AlphaStation 500 Installation 
Guide" on the web but haven't find it (i had find it in 2 online stores 
as a book but not as a free pdf document).
I was hoping that in this document i will find a list and description of 
the environment variables which can be set under the SRM Console, and 
the documentation of isp_edit. I somebody knows a good souce of 
information on these subjects please let me know.

Now, i see the following things to try:
- low level format and/or give a partition tables to each disk under 
Linux on my pc and perhaps after that they will be recognized by the Alpha ?
- do a firmware update, perhaps this could "reinitialize" something in 
the QLogic ISP1020 which block the recognition of my drives?
- Perhaps there is another thing that i don't know for adding a disk to 
an alphastation ? Actually, i plug the disk to the scsi chain and to the 
power after having set his settings with the jumpers(SCSI ID, auto-start 
(i set auto-start to true : this is not a problem?), terminator [i 
disable this function as said in the manual], i have the manual for all 
my disks [and i have read it :-)]). I should do something other ?

